# User docs — writing style

Applies when writing or editing German user docs (scope: `german-user-docs.mdc`). Reference example: [`docs/user-manual/Benutzer-Handbuch-Earnie.md`](../../docs/user-manual/Benutzer-Handbuch-Earnie.md) (edited pilot, 2026-10-17). `docs/ui/ehal-com.md` stays English; `docs/workflow/`, `docs/referenz/ehal.md`, `docs/entwicklung/` and `docs/dev/` are out of scope.

## Address and tone

- **Default: impersonal, neutral, factual — no direct address** (no „Sie“, „du“, „ihr“).
  - Instructions as infinitive steps: „Profil anlegen, danach Geräte ergänzen.“, „Container starten.“
  - Otherwise Earnie (or the page / the feature) as subject instead of passive chains: „Earnie berechnet …“, „Die Seite zeigt …“.
- **Exception — passages that invite readers to contribute** (feedback, reporting problems, usage statistics, support, community): friendly tone, address with **„Sie“**, project in the **wir** form. Examples: „Umso mehr freuen wir uns über Ihre Rückmeldungen …“, „Melden Sie sich gerne über …“, „– vielen Dank!“.
- Honest and grounded: no exaggeration or sales talk; state limits plainly („Leistungspreis … sind nicht berücksichtigt“, „keine Garantie“).
- People: prefer neutral terms („Fachbetrieb“, „Earnie-Projekt“); if persons are really meant, gender with colon („Nutzer:innen“).

## Sentences and structure

- Medium-length sentences (about 10–15 words); split long sentences and run-on paragraphs into lists.
- List items are full sentences or „**Stichwort:** erklärender Satz“, not bare keywords.
- Headings may be questions where they answer a reader's doubt („Warum weicht Historisch beim Jahresverbrauch ab?“).
- Say a fact once in the right place; elsewhere link to it instead of repeating it.
- Notes as a blockquote: `> **Hinweis:** …` (also `> **Rechenzeit:** …` etc.).
- Code identifiers, JSON keys, paths, env vars stay verbatim (`german-user-docs.mdc`); in narrative docs (handbook) put them in parentheses or at the end of a sentence, details belong in `docs/konfiguration/`.

## Mechanics

- Dash: en dash with spaces („ – “). **Never** the em dash „—“ and no dashes without spaces.
- Quotes: „…“ (German).
- „z. B.“, „u. a.“, „ggf.“ as in the existing docs; percent with space („5 %“).
- No capitals for emphasis („KEINE“, „NICHT“), no „!!!“, no emoticons or emoji. Use **bold** sparingly for the key term of a sentence.
- Avoid sentence starts with „Aber“, „Und“, „Dennoch“ — join sentences or use „Allerdings …“ sparingly.
- Avoid the rhetorical „nicht X, sondern Y“ pattern and filler phrases („Es ist wichtig zu beachten, dass …“, „nahtlos“, „ganzheitlich“).
- No internal backlog / epic IDs (`2.7.n`, `P5`, `Q8`, codenames) — see `german-user-docs.mdc`.

## Delegation: one subagent run per document

- German user docs → subagent **`docs-editor-de`** (`.cursor/agents/docs-editor-de.md`, Claude Opus 5.5, Cursor-Slug `claude-opus-5-5-medium`).
- English technical docs (`docs/referenz/ehal.md`, `DEVELOPER.md`, `docs/ui/ehal-com.md`) → subagent **`docs-editor-en`** (`.cursor/agents/docs-editor-en.md`, Claude Sonnet 5.5).
- **Start a new, separate subagent run for every document** — never pass several files to one run, never continue a previous run for the next file. The parent agent collects each report and adds suspected stale facts to `## Document Review Findings`.

## When editing an existing doc

- Change wording and structure only; **do not change facts** in the same pass. Stale or doubtful statements go to `## Document Review Findings` in `backlog/Backlog-Bugfixes.md` (skill `doc-review-findings`).
- Keep heading slugs that are link targets (`ui/doc_links.py`, inbound `#…` links); when a heading changes, add an explicit `<a id="old-slug"></a>` (skill `streamlit-doc-links`).
- After the edit run: `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m scripts.run_pytest tests/test_doc_links.py tests/test_user_docs_audience.py -q`.
